        "original_id": "f6ae0a2d-347e-56ef-8bb4-79e1d09c91ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ronnie Van Zant, Allen Collins, Steve Gaines, Cassie Gaines\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd\n- Products: Street Survivors, That Smell\n- Topics: Southern rock\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Gaines was born on September 14, 1949, and he was an American musician.\n- Steve Gaines joined Lynyrd Skynyrd on May 11, 1976 as a guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter.\n- Street Survivors is the fifth studio album by the Southern rock band Lynyrd Skynyrd, and it was released on October 17, 1977.\n- That Smell was written by Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins, and it was released in 1977 on the album Street Survivors.\n- Street Survivors is the only Lynyrd Skynyrd studio recording featuring Steve Gaines.\n- Street Survivors is the last Lynyrd Skynyrd album recorded by original members Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins.\n- Steve Gaines died on October 20, 1977.\n- Cassie Gaines was Steve Gaines's older sister, and she was a backup vocalist for Lynyrd Skynyrd's live performances.\n- Steve Gaines was a member of Lynyrd Skynyrd until his death on October 20, 1977.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
